     Notes: ConfigBot is implemented as an admin capability module, not a fake
       v24 entity. It creates validated draft packages from domain-cnc and
       design-system metadata, stores sessions/knowledge chunks through its
       repository, exposes generate/chat/reindex routes, and registers
       command-runtime handlers. Access uses `config_bot: admin`; verbal
       labels remain only permission presets. v0.1 exports virtual files only and has
       no apply/write path. Ollama is optional through deployment env vars.
       LAN host 192.168.0.67 has Ollama 0.24.0 with `qwen3:4b` and `bge-m3`
       installed, served by enabled user unit `cutkit-ollama.service`; boot
       persistence still requires user linger or a system service because sudo
       is interactive on that host. Swarm config mounts
       `/home/cutkit/Documents/cutkit-cortex` into the app at
       `/opt/cutkit-cortex` for ConfigBot reindex. Production Docker build
       also exposed and fixed Nuxt SSR relative-import issues in
       `shared/ui-permissions.js` and `test-data/factories.js`. Built and
       deployed local Swarm image `cutkit-app:configbot-v0.1`; app health is
       OK, ConfigBot routes are present behind auth, and the running container
       sees Ollama plus the cortex mount.

