    Notes:
    - Workbench fixtures now generate one interlinked CNC scenario from DTO factories and the currently compiled workflow draft.
    - Operation entity inputs use a typed entity reference selector backed by scenario refs instead of raw string-only fields.
    - Dev fixture seeding persists generated entities through a narrow workbench fixture service/repository and returns typed refs for action runs.
    - Service action input/output previews reuse `DESIGN_SYSTEM_ENTITIES` so selected refs and output artifacts render through existing entity components instead of duplicate mappings.
    - Service action parameters now support display metadata; nesting hides generated polygon/inventory payloads from normal controls and exposes `toolProfileId` as a typed `tool_profile` entity reference.
    - Service action handlers are now registered by `server/core/operations/service.js` itself, so API pages do not depend on endpoint-local side-effect imports.
    - Removed the noisy operation contract panel from Workbench; operation pages now focus on selected action, scenario controls, typed inputs, optional access override, and typed output previews.
    - Workbench test access is now global to the fixture/user context instead of per operation, and scenario access grants cassette/material/project/action permissions needed for end-to-end service action tests.
    - Moved fixture generation and global test access out of the Operations panel into a separate top-level Workbench Context tab.
    - Fixed the service action data path: `solveNesting` now creates the declared `sheet_design` output, and Workbench hydrates runtime output refs into the same entity context used by fixture data.

