    [2026-06-27] Standardize browser-local entity sync across CRUD and status
    Files changed: composables/useEntity.js, stores/entities.js,
      stores/entities.spec.js, utils/entity-events.js,
      utils/entity-events.spec.js
    Docs updated: composables/README.md, stores/README.md, utils/README.md,
      TODO.org
    Notes: Successful `useEntity()` create/update/delete now emit the same
      entity sync contract as status transitions, and the shared entity cache
      consumes that contract automatically. This standardizes in-browser entity
      refresh behavior around one event shape instead of per-feature callbacks.

    [2026-06-27] Add cross-device entity event bus
    Files changed: server/features/entity-events/service.js,
      server/features/entity-events/entity-events.spec.js,
      server/api/entity-events/index.get.js,
      server/api/entity-events/index.post.js,
      server/api/status/transition.post.js, composables/useEntity.js,
      composables/useGeneratedScreen.js,
      server/features/process-definitions/service.js,
      stores/entityEvents.js, stores/entityEvents.spec.js,
      stores/entities.js, layouts/app.vue
    Docs updated: server/README.md, server/features/README.md,
      server/features/entity-events/README.md, server/api/README.md,
      server/features/process-definitions/README.md, composables/README.md,
      stores/README.md, utils/README.md, scripts/README.md, TODO.org
    Notes: Added an authenticated in-memory SSE invalidation bus for entity
      changes. Status transitions publish server events directly, successful
      frontend CRUD mutations publish after their canonical API call succeeds,
      generated process actions publish from the process runtime, and the app
      shell bridges incoming server events into the existing browser-local
      entity sync contract so generated screens and shared listeners refresh
      across devices.
      expose and sent refs no longer disappear during send-time normalization.
      Support attachment source discovery now ignores generated `single` detail
      sources, so entity pickers stay aligned with generated list windows
      instead of widening through detail routes. Entity type and option
      endpoints now resolve sender process auth before deriving generated chat
      scopes, so the live API matches the current process manifest instead of
      falling back to raw session auth. `entity-options` now follows the same
      first readable generated source that `entity-types` exposes for each
      entity type, preventing hidden multi-source unions and duplicate option
      rows behind a single picker label. Chat-only recipient refs now avoid
      protected inline refetches when an older message lacks a stored entity
      snapshot, and cassette snapshots keep preview-driving fields so new
      direct-chat inline previews render without a fallback fetch. Older
      non-restricted cassette refs still rehydrate through the normal entity
      API when their stored snapshot predates that richer preview contract.
      Support write validation now normalizes frontend entity-type aliases such
      as `cassetteDesign` and `nestingRun` to canonical backend snake-case
      types before checking generated attachment scope, which prevents draft
      refs from disappearing on send. The chat composer also posts only compact
      `{ type, id, label }` refs on send instead of the hydrated entity objects
      used for draft preview rendering. Composer type labels are now localized
      on the client, and attachment-only messages are allowed as long as at
      least one entity ref survives send-time validation.

