      keeping project-scoped queues when projectId is provided. Queue numbering
      counts within either project scope or organization-root scope. Process
      compilation again exposes root queue create actions after stripping stale
      invalid parents, and active process definitions were recompiled so
      Montage can run the queue create action without a project prompt.

    [2026-06-24] Hide create actions with unresolved lineage parents
    Files changed: packages/processes/src/index.js,
      packages/processes/src/index.spec.js
    Docs updated: packages/processes/README.md, TODO.org
    Notes: Queue creation failed with "Project ID is required" because the
      active action still stored a stale cassette parent; compilation stripped
      that unsupported parent to a root queue action. Create actions with a
      required domain lineage parent are now omitted from role action manifests
      unless the process graph provides a valid parent. Stale exposed
      construction sockets still normalize through the domain construction
      contract. Recompiled active process definitions after the change; the
      stale queue create action is no longer assigned to Montage or any user
      action manifest. Superseded later the same day by organization-root queue
      creation support, which makes root queue actions valid again.

