     [2026-06-17] Restore cassette hardware contour helper
     Files changed: utils/occs/hardware.js, utils/cassetteV2Renderer.js,
       utils/cassetteV2FoldedPreview.js, utils/cassetteV2Renderer.spec.js,
       components/CassetteDesignerV2.vue, i18n/locales/en.json,
       i18n/locales/ru.json, utils/occs/README.md, TODO.org
     Docs updated: utils/occs/README.md, TODO.org
     Notes: Restored the pure OCCS hardware helper required by
       cassetteV2Renderer's cut-hanger path. The helper normalizes declarative
       hardware families and hanger production modes, expands edge-array
       placement points, generates integral-cut hanger polygons for `cut.inner`,
       and resolves hole hardware diameters for `cut.hole`. Verified renderer,
       folded preview, clipper, and OCCS drawing tests covering boolean-shaped
       parent faces and production layer dispatch. Follow-up fixes keep
       fold-route indexing on preserved original face boundaries after hanger
       booleans, expose start/end snap bindings, and make hardware edge arrays
       respect start/end/center binding with X as a two-sided edge margin.
       Designer section helper lines now render on `designer.section` instead
       of leaking into the production `code.cassette_mark` layer.
       Edge-breaking integral hanger cuts are now boolean-only operands: they
       alter the parent `cut.outer` contour and are not emitted as `cut.inner`,
       OCCS cut entities, or folded-preview cutout wires.
       Whole-workpiece assembly preview now dispatches `contour.cassette_face`,
       `cut.outer`, and `fold.route` from the same per-workpiece production
       layout used by face-selected preview instead of raw per-face paths.

