  [2026-07-18 Sat 12:12]
  Everywhere in app, where dropdowns use cutkit entities, need to replace select element content with entity card (compact variant with preview), and selected items are displayed also as compact entity cards instead of having an input in select trigger with selected items as badges.

** Implementation plan

   1. Add shared =EntitySelect= and =EntityMultiSelect= wrappers around
      PrimeVue controls. They must preserve the complete ordinary Select API
      and slots for scalar options, but render canonical entity options and
      selected values through =EntityInlineRef variant="compact"=.
   2. Resolve entity DTOs from either raw canonical options or
      ={ label, value, entity }= option records. Resolve entity type explicitly
      from the picker contract or the option record; do not infer entity type
      from mutable data/status values.
   3. Replace direct PrimeVue Select/MultiSelect imports with the shared
      wrappers throughout app UI so entity behavior is architectural rather
      than page-specific. Mark every actual entity picker with its entity type;
      leave scalar/enum/role/process-record selectors behaviorally unchanged.
   4. Replace the existing =EntityRefInput= custom option/value markup with the
      shared wrapper contract and add focused resolver/component-contract tests.
   5. Document the picker pattern, validate all changed Vue SFCs, run focused
      design-system/localization tests, synchronize the framework manifest when
      required, and commit implementation/docs separately.

** Execution notes

   - Added shared =EntitySelect= and =EntityMultiSelect= primitives. They own
     the only direct PrimeVue Select/MultiSelect imports in app UI, preserve
     non-entity props/events/slots, and use non-interactive compact entity cards
     for entity options and selected values.
   - Migrated typed entity selectors for queues, machines, tools, cassette
     designs/templates, profile templates, materials, layer standards, pens,
     warehouses, catalogs, colors, users, process definitions, and generated
     entity input fields. Scalar/enum/role selectors continue through the same
     wrappers without entity rendering.
   - Registered both primitives in the domain design-system contract and UI
     lab, regenerated =framework.manifest.json=, and added resolver/component
     contract coverage including an ownership scan that rejects direct app
     PrimeVue Select/MultiSelect imports.
   - Validation: 55 focused tests passed; all 180 app Vue SFCs compiled;
     =npm run framework:validate=, =npm run framework:manifest=,
     =node scripts/check-arch.js=, and =git diff --check= passed.
     =shared/localization.spec.js= retains only the three pre-existing missing
     keys outside this task: =nesting.selectMachine=, =nesting.thickness=, and
     =common.rotate=.

** Follow-up repair

   - Integrated the picker branch into the primary =local= checkout after
     preserving both sides of the pre-existing additive TODO merge conflict.
   - Fixed library-to-queue cassette design construction: immutable revision
     identities now include the source entity id, so first geometry revisions
     from different cassette templates cannot collide and leave provenance
     without a source.
   - Active process hydration now supplies its compiled workflows to shared
     entity surfaces. Status chrome is hidden when the effective lifecycle has
     exactly one unique state, while the canonical status block remains stored.
   - Corrected the entity-picker selection layout: Select and MultiSelect keep
     only their chooser placeholder inside the PrimeVue control and render
     selected compact entity refs in a separate region below it. This replaces
     the previous value-slot implementation that still embedded selected cards
     inside the input surface.
   - Validation: 50 focused picker/design-system tests passed; both picker SFCs
     compiled; =npm run framework:validate=, the regenerated manifest check,
     and =git diff --check= passed.

** Follow-up repair

   - Repaired the selected-state trigger layout for =EntitySelect= and
     =EntityMultiSelect=. Selected compact entity refs now render outside and
     before the PrimeVue control, while the bound PrimeVue control remains as a
     compact change trigger with a real icon value and selected-label
     accessibility text. This avoids empty value slots and prevents the selected
     state from becoming a zero-height full-width input.
   - Updated the focused wrapper spec to assert the compact trigger, outside
     selection region, and unselected full chooser behavior.
   - Updated shared component/design-system documentation and primitive
     metadata to describe the compact change-trigger contract.
* WAITING Architecture repair execution plan
  :PROPERTIES:
  :ID: architecture-repair-execution-plan-2026-07-15
  :ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-08-06 Thu 09:45
  :ARCHIVE_FILE: /home/isuo/Projects/cutkit-demo/TODO.org
  :ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: TODO
  :ARCHIVE_TODO: WAITING
  :END:

  Review status: blocking relations/provenance feedback incorporated;
  implementation completed and validated on 2026-07-15.
  This plan replaces the two reverted implementation attempts and treats the
  current =local= tree as the only implementation baseline.

** Summary

   Implement all ten tasks as one coordinated contract migration. Replace
   hardcoded queue/UI behavior with process-compiled capabilities, separate
   entity containment from ordinary links, add revision-aware references,
   introduce machine profiles, consolidate entity mutation, and normalize
   nesting output by cassette composition.

   Infrastructure must not hardcode organization lifecycle states. Active
   organizations use their compiled process workflows and the Status engine.
   Domain workflow defaults apply only when no active organization process
   exists, or for genuinely system-owned runtime mechanics.

** Public contracts and architecture

*** Entity relations and containment

    - Extend =@cutkit/core= with one canonical =EntityRef= value:
      ={ type, id, revisionId? }=. The optional revision ID identifies an
      immutable =entity_revision= for that same source entity. Runtime results,
      process ports, relations, and provenance use this exact value shape.
    - Add canonical =relations= and =provenance= entity blocks. A relation entry
      contains one =EntityRef= or a cardinality-declared list of =EntityRef=
      values. A provenance entry contains a =source: EntityRef= plus immutable
      derivation facts such as scope, revision number, content hash, source
      status, and parameters.
    - Use =relations= for non-owning links such as a project using a cassette
      library. Relations must not affect ownership, access ancestry, top-level
      list placement, or breadcrumbs.
    - Use =provenance= for immutable derivation evidence and for an optional
      exact immediate-parent revision captured at child creation. Provenance is
      never an editable relation and never changes containment or access.
    - Reserve =lineage= for containment and access ancestry.
    - Replace =cncSummaries= as the implicit parent/child registry with explicit
      containment declarations containing parent type, child type, lineage key,
      and optional aggregate policy. Keep summary aggregation separate.
    - Add process-authored relation declarations to entity profiles so relation
      sockets, traversal, persistence, and display derive from one contract.

*** Revision-aware references

    - Keep scalar =lineage.<parentType>Id= fields for access and queries.
    - When child creation pins the immediate parent revision, store
      =provenance.parent.source = { type, id, revisionId }=. The =type= and =id=
      must match the declared containment parent and the scalar lineage parent
      ID. Never add revision keys to =lineage= and never encode composite IDs
      with delimiters.
    - Ordinary relations may independently pin a revision through the same
      optional =EntityRef.revisionId= field.
    - No revision means follow the entity; a revision means reproduce the
      relationship against that exact immutable snapshot.
    - Migrate cassette-design derivation from =data.derivedFrom= to
      =provenance.derivedFrom= and entity-revision source metadata from sibling
      =entityType/entityId= fields to =data.source: { type, id }=. Do not retain
      dual-read compatibility paths after migration.

*** Machine, tool, material, and queue settings

    - Add a =machine= entity with public system records and organization-owned
      records.
    - Seed a system default with a 3000 x 1500 mm working area and zero uniform
      sheet-boundary offset.
    - Replace queue nesting spacing/settings with explicit =machineId=,
      =toolProfileId=, material mode/source references, and virtual material
      width, length, and thickness.
    - The selected tool's =kerf= is the exact nesting and manual-editor item
      gap. Remove the independent spacing override and do not retain a fallback.
    - Nesting runs store immutable serialized machine, tool, and material
      snapshots. The strict worker payload is derived from those snapshots.
    - Reserve ordinary OCCS parameter =T= for selected material thickness.
      Queue material selection injects =T= into parametric cassette items;
      queue item editing cannot override it independently.

*** Process actions

    - Replace separate =changeStatus= actions with one canonical =updateEntity=
      action kind and migrate stored process definitions.
    - Derive the action's entity type, writable block/field/relation sockets,
      and output entity type live from the connected entity profile.
    - Rewrite only connected sockets. A connected status socket calls the
      Status engine and never patches the status block as ordinary data.
    - Extend compiled action manifests with normalized entity input/output
      contracts. Consumers derive capabilities from those contracts, not from
      action IDs, labels, or UI-local lists.

** Implementation by task

*** Task 1: cassette-aware sheet editing

    - Replace grid-coordinate snapping with magnetic snapping against other
      transformed cassette production contours/bounds.
    - Generate candidate translations at exactly the selected tool kerf and
      reject candidates that overlap or violate minimum clearance.
    - Clamp placements to the usable sheet polygon after machine boundary
      offset. Keep the grid visual only; it no longer controls placement.
    - Add a selected-placement rotate control that rotates exactly 90 degrees
      in the canonical worker rotation unit, then recomputes bounds, snapping,
      and clamping before persistence.

*** Task 2: artifact-first camera/upload flow

    - Bring artifacts fully onto the backend Golden Path: authenticated
      create/list/detail/delete services, repository-owned persistence and file
      cleanup, workflow-derived initial status, access filtering, DTO
      serialization, and entity invalidation.
    - Generated attachment inputs support ordinary upload and camera capture.
      Both persist the immutable file and create an artifact entity first.
    - Geometry capture consumes an artifact reference instead of owning a
      separately uploaded photo. DXF cassette import likewise consumes an
      artifact before producing a cassette design.

*** Task 3: generated queue composition and run presentation

    - Add typed cassette-design producer contracts for baking a readable
      cassette template, importing a DXF artifact, and selecting an existing
      readable cassette design.
    - Any future process action or entity source whose compiled output is
      =cassette_design=, including a future facade flow, automatically qualifies
      without a QueueEditor change.
    - In active-process mode, populate the queue's add-design menu only from
      producer actions and readable sources in the user's compiled manifest.
      Outside process mode, use the domain/system manifest rather than
      hardcoded Vue controls.
    - Library-backed creation resolves readable cassette templates through the
      declared project/library relation and normal access policy.
    - Remove the hardcoded cassette/template selector and DXF upload button.
      Append successful producer outputs through the canonical queue update
      boundary as ={ id, entityType: "cassette_design", quantity, parameters }=.
    - Keep =nesting_run= as a child entity rather than a queue revision because
      it is an independently actionable async attempt with parameters, status,
      failure history, and selection provenance.
    - Present runs through one selector and render sheet designs only for the
      currently selected run. Project production output continues to show only
      the accepted run.

*** Tasks 4 and 6: hierarchy and non-owning links

    - Make parent-bound creation require the parent, inherit complete ancestry,
      optionally record =provenance.parent= with the configured parent revision,
      and publish the child via normal entity events.
    - Generated top-level sources exclude rows carrying a declared parent
      lineage key. The same entity type may still have both root records and
      child records.
    - Generated parent details derive child sources and child create actions
      from containment declarations, never from summary counters.
    - Add relation sockets to entity/update nodes. Connecting a related entity
      writes the declared =relations= entry without changing containment.
    - Implement project-to-library as the first explicit non-owning relation and
      render it through shared entity relation primitives.
    - Make related-entity traversal nodes select a declared relation key and
      cardinality rather than only an unconstrained target type.

*** Task 5: revision-pinned containment evidence and relations

    - Keep lineage construction unchanged as the cumulative ancestor-ID map.
      When configured, parent-bound creation resolves the parent's current
      immutable revision and records it in =provenance.parent.source=.
    - Expose revision pinning in process authoring and display pinned revisions
      through shared revision/entity reference UI.
    - Move existing ad hoc derivation records to canonical provenance without
      turning them into relations. Migrate editable non-owning links to canonical
      relations separately.

*** Task 7: composition-based sheet designs and sheet twins

    - Collapse worker layouts by cassette composition multiset only: sorted
      cassette-design IDs plus each design's count.
    - Geometry, placement order, material, and machine data do not split equal
      compositions. The first layout in stable worker order becomes the
      representative editable geometry.
    - Create one =sheet_design= per unique composition and store its composition
      hash and aggregate sheet count.
    - At nesting completion, create one =sheet= entity per collapsed quantity,
      linked through sheet-design, run, queue, and project lineage.
    - Resolve each new sheet's initial state from the active organization's
      compiled sheet workflow. The nesting task emits facts and entity refs but
      never names or forces an organization lifecycle state.
    - Run selection binds material sources to existing sheet twins instead of
      creating duplicates. Later lifecycle movement occurs only through
      process-defined update/status wiring.
    - Remove hardcoded queue/run/sheet state checks from orchestration wherever
      process intents or compiled actions own the decision.

*** Task 8: machine/material/OCCS nesting flow

    - Register the machine feature, service/repository/model, APIs, access
      policy, system seed, organization CRUD, frontend metadata, and generated
      entity surfaces.
    - Validate that selected material dimensions fit the selected machine
      working area.
    - Convert machine boundary offset to the worker's usable =sheet_polygon=
      while preserving full physical sheet dimensions on runs/designs/sheets.
    - Warehouse material supplies width, length, and thickness from canonical
      specs. Virtual material requires all three before nesting.
    - Resolve machine and tool entities before enqueueing and serialize exact
      values into the run snapshot. Derive worker =space= only from tool kerf.
    - Ensure default OCCS cassette templates declare =T=, baking evaluates it as
      an ordinary numeric parameter, and material changes propagate =T= to all
      parametric queue items. Static imported designs remain fixed geometry.

*** Task 9: unified mutation and process designer repair

    - Migrate every stored =changeStatus= action to =updateEntity= with a status
      input while preserving grants, transition windows, evidence contracts,
      authored display metadata, and graph edges.
    - Expose one typed entity input, canonical writable replacement-block
      sockets, lifecycle status, and one typed result. Leaf field sockets stay
      on Compose/Modify Block so entity persistence does not duplicate block
      algebra or manufacture entity-owned block schemas.
    - Resolve graph values and validate field policy, block membership, open
      entry type qualifiers, access, and lifecycle contracts before delegating
      block replacement and status changes to their owning runtime boundaries.
      Status is never patched as ordinary entity data.
    - Repair block algebra so entity decomposition emits every canonical block,
      field readers consume one typed block, block composers assemble typed
      block patches, and update actions assemble the final entity patch from
      connected values only.
    - Remove obsolete action/node kinds during migration instead of preserving
      adapters.
    - Refactor the designer with existing design-system primitives: compact
      typed nodes/sockets, one entity-update palette item, reusable status value
      nodes, dense configuration in the selected-node inspector, localized
      labels, and typed edge validation.

*** Task 10: hierarchical navigation breadcrumbs

    - Make route breadcrumbs and =TraceChain= consume the same containment
      resolver.
    - Render hub, each accessible ancestor, and the current entity in order.
    - Resolve sibling menus within the same parent scope.
    - Use compiled generated detail routes in process mode and enforce the same
      access checks as entity screens. Ordinary relations never appear as
      ancestry.

** Migration and rollout

   - Add a dry-run/apply migration for artifact records backing existing
     geometry-capture photos and DXF uploads, then replace those consumers with
     artifact relations.
   - Migrate =data.derivedFrom= records into canonical provenance,
     =entity_revision.data.entityType/entityId= into =data.source=, editable
     non-owning links into relations, and any revision-like lineage fields into
     =provenance.parent=. Remove the old shapes after apply.
   - Migrate =changeStatus= process actions to unified updates and recompile all
     active process contracts before removing the old compiled shape.
   - Backfill existing run layout composition metadata non-destructively,
     report duplicate compositions for review, and create missing sheet twins
     without deleting historical sheet designs, revisions, or references.
   - Move queue settings to machine/tool/material contracts. Assign the seeded
     system machine when missing. Queues without a tool or material thickness
     remain editable drafts but nesting is rejected until the required values
     are selected; old spacing is not read as a fallback.
   - Reject activation of a process that exposes nesting without accessible
     =nesting_run=, =sheet_design=, and =sheet= output profiles/workflows.
   - Update all affected architecture, feature, process, component, OCCS, and
     script READMEs in the implementation session. Add completion notes to the
     ten tasks only after implementation and validation actually succeed.

** Validation and acceptance

*** Relationship and navigation coverage

    - Root and child records of the same type route to the correct generated
      source.
    - Child creation inherits ancestry and optionally records an exact parent
      revision in provenance without adding a lineage revision field.
    - Linked libraries do not become children or change access lineage.
    - Child regions, root filters, relation traversal, TraceChain, and route
      breadcrumbs use the same declarations.

*** Artifact and queue coverage

    - Upload and camera-shaped payloads create artifacts first.
    - Geometry and DXF processing consume artifact refs.
    - Artifact list/detail/delete access is consistent and file cleanup remains
      service-owned.
    - Only manifest-exposed cassette-design producers appear in process mode.
    - Template, artifact import, existing design, and future generic producer
      outputs append canonical queue items; unauthorized actions never appear.
    - Only the selected run's sheets are rendered.

*** Nesting and sheet coverage

    - Tool kerf is the sole item gap.
    - Machine/material snapshots are immutable and worker payloads use the
      usable offset polygon.
    - Missing tool or thickness blocks execution.
    - Equal cassette composition collapses regardless of placement geometry.
    - Sheet twin count equals collapsed multiplicity.
    - No executor writes organization lifecycle literals.
    - Neighbor snapping preserves kerf clearance, rejects overlap, honors
      usable sheet polygons plus boundary offset, and keeps four successive
      rotations reversible/in-bounds.

*** Process and OCCS coverage

    - Migrated status actions retain access, workflow, display, and evidence
      semantics.
    - Only connected fields change; validation failures leave entity and status
      history unchanged, and combined mutations require Mongo transaction
      support before any status history/entity patch write is accepted.
    - Decompose/read/compose/update port combinations round-trip and reject
      incompatible connections.
    - =T= evaluates in OCCS templates/designs and changes with selected material
      thickness without creating aliases or overrides.

*** Required commands

    - Run focused Vitest suites while implementing.
    - Run =node scripts/check-arch.js=.
    - Run =npm run framework:validate=.
    - Run design-system and framework package specs.
    - Run OCCS evaluator, renderer, and toolkit checks.
    - Run process compiler/runtime suites and migration integrity checks.
    - Run focused Playwright workflows when the existing app stack is available.
    - Do not run =npm run build= or start a development server.

** Locked decisions and assumptions

   - Same sheet design means the same cassette-design/count multiset. The first
     worker layout is the canonical representative.
   - Active organization processes are authoritative for lifecycle states.
     Infrastructure must not introduce a =PLANNED= or other business state.
   - A nesting run remains an entity rather than an entity revision.
   - Machine boundary offset is a uniform inset in millimeters.
   - Tool kerf, not diameter or a queue override, defines nesting and snapping
     clearance.
   - =T= is the reserved material-thickness parameter and is material-bound.
   - Upload/camera creation produces an artifact before downstream processing.
   - Active-process queue inputs come only from the compiled process manifest.

** Agent Notes

*** [2026-07-15] Architecture repair implementation attempt invalidated by review

    The previous completion note was inaccurate. Follow-up review found blocking
    implementation defects: destructive sheet-design migration, parametric
    =T= changes not re-baking geometry, process definitions writing foreign
    feature collections, transaction-only combined mutations on the checked-in
    standalone Mongo topology, false validation reporting, and incomplete
    canonical block documentation.

*** [2026-07-15] Corrective repair after review

    Corrective implementation scope:
    - Sheet-design composition migration is non-destructive: it backfills
      metadata, reports duplicate compositions, and creates missing sheet twins
      without deleting historical designs, revisions, or references.
    - Parametric queue items whose queued parameters differ from saved baked
      geometry are evaluated from the source cassette provenance during nesting,
      including material-bound =T= changes, without persisting duplicate
      cassette designs or DXFs.
    - Process-definition runtime no longer performs generic collection reads or
      writes for business entities. Parent context is passed to owning feature
      create services, and non-status updates delegate to owning feature
      =update()= methods.
    - Combined status/entity mutations require Mongo transactions; standalone
      Mongo rejects those combined mutations instead of using partial ordered
      writes.
    - Machine contracts include required origin/status blocks, and public
      canonical block docs include relations/provenance.
    - Queue composition UI exposes existing cassette designs by real
      =cassette_designs:read= permission and accepts process producers only
      from current =contracts.outputs= compiled output contracts.
    - Sheet-editor snapping uses axis-aligned neighbor bounds, kerf clearance,
      transformed-polygon overlap checks, and rectangular rotated-boundary
      clamping.

    Validation report superseded:
    - Follow-up review found the claimed framework/package validation was not
      reproducible. Treat the validation list from this note as invalidated;
      see the subsequent repair note for the corrected validation record.

*** [2026-07-15] Follow-up repair after review findings

    Corrective implementation scope:
    - Kept composition-based sheet-design collapse as the locked requirement
      and corrected nesting/sheet-design docs that still described one design
      per physical layout.
    - Replaced persistent parametric nesting re-bake with request-local source
      cassette evaluation, so material-bound =T= changes update worker geometry
      without creating duplicate =cassette_design= rows or GridFS DXFs.
    - Restored =solveNesting= execution grants to cassette/cassette-design read
      access only.
    - Removed QueueEditor's legacy output-shape fallback; process producers now
      require current =contracts.outputs=.
    - Removed the invalid generic non-status feature-service update call.
      Non-status process updates now fail unless an owning feature
