      =GeneratedRegion.vue=, =QueueEditor.vue=, =GeneratedEntityDetail.vue=,
      and =QueueEntryCard.vue= passed.

*** [2026-07-15] Queue producer append repair after browser failure

    Follow-up browser feedback showed that generated cassette-design actions
    still did not appear or append in the queue composer for process-scoped
    users. Root causes:
    - =GeneratedEntityDetail= only forwarded queue producers from screen/region
      action ids, while queue composition producers are current user-manifest
      actions whose =contracts.outputs= exposes =cassette_design=.
    - =QueueEditor= still hid Add and blocked =addEntry()/saveQueue()= behind
      raw =queues:write=, so process producer actions could create a design but
      not add it to the queue.
    - Queue item panel headers still rendered an embedded relation ref card
      instead of a simple row identity.

    Corrective implementation:
    - Queue detail now passes manifest-exposed cassette-design producer actions
      into =QueueEditor= while keeping normal generated header/action buttons
      screen-scoped.
    - Process-mode producer execution sends queue context plus
      =queueAppend.quantity= to the active process action endpoint. The server
      appends the produced =cassette_design= through the queue feature's
      explicit =processUpdate()= boundary with a narrow action-scoped queue
      write grant, then emits queue invalidation. The browser refreshes queue
      data instead of calling the generic queue PATCH path.
    - Existing-design selection remains available only when the user has a real
      queue write grant; no frontend compatibility fallback for obsolete
      =outputs= shapes was added.
    - Queue item headers now render the hydrated cassette-design identity or a
      typed id chip, not an inline relation card.

*** [2026-07-15] Existing cassette-design source append repair

    Follow-up audit found the previous repair still left one Task 3 source
    incomplete: process-scoped users could run generated cassette-design
    producer actions, but selecting an existing readable =cassette_design=
    still required raw =queues:write= and therefore did not satisfy the
    readable entity-source path.

    Corrective implementation:
    - Added an active-process queue item endpoint for existing design sources.
      It loads the readable queue and readable cassette design through their
      owning feature services, then appends the canonical queue item through
      queue =processUpdate()= with a narrow request-local queue write grant.
    - =QueueEditor= now shows the existing-design source in process mode when
      the user can read cassette designs, and posts that selection to the
      active-process queue item endpoint before refreshing queue data.
    - Updated stale queue UI docs that still described screen-scoped producers
      and inline relation-card row headers.

*** [2026-07-15] Process assignment legacy status-action compile repair

    Browser/E2E setup exposed that registering or assigning a user into the
    active process still failed when the semantic process source contained old
    =changeStatus= actions. Auth hydration had an in-memory repair, but
    =assignUserToActiveProcessInternal()= recompiled the active semantic source
    directly and therefore raised unknown action-kind errors before Playwright
    could exercise the generated queue detail UI.

    Corrective implementation:
    - Active process assignment now applies the feature-local
      =changeStatus= -> =updateEntity= normalizer before validating role ids
      and recompiling. Because assignment persists the active process, this
      also stores the canonical semantic action kind instead of repeatedly
      relying on runtime hydration repair.
    - Added service coverage proving a legacy status action compiles into a
      current =updateEntity= action with strict =contracts.inputs= and
      =contracts.outputs= after assignment.

    Validation:
    - =npx vitest run server/features/process-definitions/process-definitions.spec.js=
      passed: 1 file, 23 tests.

*** [2026-07-15] Generated queue producer default-template UI repair

    Playwright against the generated queue detail showed that =Add Entry= was
    visible and the manifest-generated =Create cassette design= option was
    present, but the action dialog kept =Add= disabled when the process role
    could not list cassette templates. The server-side
    =bakeCassetteDesignFromTemplate= action already supports resolving the
    default constructable cassette template, so the UI was stricter than the
    process action contract.

    Corrective implementation:
    - In process mode, QueueEditor now omits an empty/unreadable
      =templateId= selector for =bakeCassetteDesignFromTemplate= producers and
      treats that field as satisfied, allowing the server action to resolve the
      default template.
    - When no template-specific parameter list is visible, QueueEditor still
      sends current material thickness as =T= so material-bound generated
      designs receive the queue nesting thickness.

    Validation:
    - Vue SFC parse check for =components/QueueEditor.vue= passed.
    - Playwright against
      =/screens/auto_queue_detail?entityId=q-EI1Vtn51= found exactly one
      accessible =Add Entry= button, verified it opened the
      =Create cassette design Создано= producer menu, and captured the primary
      in-grid button surface.
    - Playwright against
      =/screens/auto_queue_detail?entityId=q-EI1Vtn51= as a process-role user
      showed =Add Entry= enabled, the =Create cassette design= producer
      option visible, the template selector omitted when unreadable, and the
      final =Add= button enabled after entering a design name.

*** [2026-07-15] Entity revision stale-index execution repair

    Full Playwright execution of the generated cassette-design producer reached
    the process action endpoint but failed while creating the cassette geometry
    revision. The local database still had the old
    =entity_revision_content_hash= index name on
    =(data.entityType, data.entityId, data.scope, data.contentHash)=, while the
    current repository creates the same named index on
    =(data.source.type, data.source.id, data.scope, data.contentHash)=.
    Mongo rejected the duplicate name/key mismatch before the design could be
    persisted.

    Corrective implementation:
    - Entity revision index setup now compares existing named index keys and
      drops/recreates the content/latest indexes when an older database has the
      same index name on the pre-source-key shape.
    - Revision hash/latest lookups, DTO serialization, and derived provenance
      now read both current =data.source= records and existing
      =data.entityType/entityId= records so old snapshots can still be reused
      without producing invalid provenance.
    - Entity revision docs now describe the current =data.source= index
      contract instead of the old =data.entityType/entityId= fields.

    Validation:
    - Added repository coverage for replacing the stale index and keeping the
      current one unchanged, plus legacy revision source/provenance coverage.
    - Full Playwright execution of the generated queue producer returned 200
      from
      =/api/process-definitions/active/actions/action_1782325155992/execute=
      and refreshed the queue row list with =E2E generated design 4=.
    - =node scripts/check-arch.js= passed with the existing non-blocking
      migration inventory.

*** [2026-07-15] Queue composer visible add and legacy row display repair

    Follow-up browser review showed the generated queue composer did have an
    =Add Entry= action, but it was only a small panel-header control. In the
    visible cassette grid this was too easy to miss and did not read as the
    primary interface for adding cassettes/designs to the queue. The same queue
    also contained an old explicit =entityType: cassette= parametric item, so
    the row appeared as a raw id when the referenced template was not readable
    to the process role.

    Corrective implementation:
    - =QueueEditor= now renders an in-grid =Add Entry= tile in addition to the
      panel-header action whenever process/generated producers are available.
    - Queue item resolution now hydrates explicit legacy
