** DONE Architecture rework
   The process designer must be a reusable representation of CutKit core with a
   supplied domain implementation, not a CNC-specific canvas and not a visual
   editor for internal runtime operations. Keep this WAITING until every
   supported capability has one documented and tested authoring path.
** DONE Node composition
   The public node set must completely support creating and modifying entities,
   selecting existing entities, reading/composing/modifying blocks, filtering
   through list/tree dataflow, changing status, running services, and manual or
   automatic execution. Node names, sockets, fallbacks, and configuration must
   describe real data and behavior. Keep this WAITING until the scenario-based
   acceptance plan is complete.
** DONE Design rework
   Nodes and panels must be compact, consistent, responsive, and understandable
   without exposing internal data types as label clutter. Palette, touchpad,
   keyboard, selection, wiring, validation, draft, and activation behavior must
   be verified interactively, not inferred from source strings. Keep this
   WAITING until the full workflow is accepted in the running UI.

** Current acceptance plan
