  [2026-07-18 Sat 10:37]
  Need to upload org-scoped templates in dxf/pdf and process them, store, and make artifact generation process to use optional template. Template needs to be customizable (different text fields should be parametrized and inserted in resulting artifacts); example: text field in uploaded one should be chosen as variable, and should be assigned, both automatic in process designer or by hand. Artifact geometry should be editable too, as revisions: move/delete placed items.

** Implementation plan

   1. Introduce =artifact_template= as an organization-scoped canonical entity.
      Its source file remains an attachment; normalized pages/entities, declared
      typed variables, and the active layout revision are entity data. Register
      the entity, access policy, endpoints, runtime service, UI contract, and
      entity-revision scope through the existing domain and Golden Path
      registries.

   2. Implement DXF/PDF template ingestion through the template-owning feature.
      Validate the uploaded media type, persist the source safely, extract DXF
      text/geometry or PDF page/text metadata into one normalized layout
      contract, create the initial immutable layout revision, and clean up the
      stored file if entity creation fails.

   3. Implement template customization as revision-backed layout replacement.
      Editors can mark extracted text items as named typed variables, change
      their defaults, and move or delete layout items. Updates create/deduplicate
      an =entity_revision= snapshot and move the template's active revision
      pointer; revision records themselves remain immutable.

   4. Replace the inert =pdfTemplateId= metadata field in
      =generateAttachment= with an optional typed =artifact_template= input and
      a values object. Validate values against the selected template's variable
      declarations, render DXF/PDF output from the pinned template revision,
      store the resulting file, and record source/template revision provenance
      on the generated artifact. Generation without a template must keep the
      existing native layout-DXF behavior.

   5. Expose the command inputs consistently to process and manual execution.
      Process-designer command sockets must include the optional template entity
      and values data; generated manual action dialogs must render command
      parameter/entity inputs instead of silently running with empty parameters.
      Connected process data and manually entered values must reach the same
      command contract without hardcoded status or entity-specific UI logic.

   6. Replace the placeholder assets/templates page with the design-system
      management surface: organization-scoped list, DXF/PDF upload, source
      preview, variable selection/editing, item move/delete controls, revision
      save, and access-controlled delete. Keep user-visible strings localized
      and use shared page/dialog/entity primitives.

   7. Migrate stored process action inputs from the removed =pdfTemplateId=
      parameter to the new template entity/value contract, update architecture
      documentation, and validate focused feature/API/rendering/process/UI
      tests plus =node scripts/check-arch.js= and
      =npm run framework:validate=.

** Completion

   - Added the organization-scoped =artifact_template= Golden Path feature,
     DXF/PDF source ingestion, normalized editable layouts, typed text
     variables, immutable template/artifact layout revisions, and pinned
     template-revision provenance on generated artifacts.
   - Replaced =pdfTemplateId= with typed command inputs for the optional
     template entity and values. Process-designer sockets and generated manual
     dialogs now project the same current command contract. The stored-process
     migration was applied and its final dry run scanned 100 definitions with
     =changed: 0=.
   - Replaced the assets/templates placeholder with the design-system template
     manager and reused the layout editor for generated artifacts. Create,
     update, and delete controls derive visibility from process access grants.
   - Revision creation now resolves its status through the workflow service;
     the registered =entity_revision= fallback is the terminal system state
     =RECORDED=, not a feature-service status literal.

   Validation:
   - Focused Vitest: 10 files, 140 tests passed.
   - =node scripts/check-arch.js= passed.
   - =npm run framework:validate= passed.
   - =npm run framework:manifest= and the isolated manifest synchronization
     spec passed.
   - Six changed Vue SFCs, both locale JSON files, and =git diff --check=
     passed.
   - =shared/localization.spec.js= still reports seven pre-existing missing
     keys in QueueEditor, SheetDesignEditor, and the process designer; none are
     introduced by this task.
