** Execution notes

   - Added a generated overload registry in =components/generated/overloads.js=.
     Default app overloads are resolved after the effective user screen manifest
     is composed and source states are loaded, so overload components only see
     screen sources/actions/regions available to the current user.
   - Moved queue and sheet-design generated detail bodies into the registry
     instead of hardcoded branches in =GeneratedEntityDetail=.
   - Added =GeneratedProjectWorkspace.vue= for project =entityDetail= screens.
     It renders a bounded IDE-style Explorer plus recursively split file panes;
     there is no permanently reserved inspector. The project file is an
     operational launcher for current-user compiled direct-child creation and
     relation/attachment actions rather than a duplicate project summary.
     Ordinary entity/lifecycle actions remain in the file-header ellipsis.
     Child files render their pane-native detail overload, including the real
     queue editor.
   - Queue files give the composition editor the full pane when no
     nesting-run/support region is visible. Queue-entry cards use compact,
     card-container-responsive preview and control layouts. Canonical persisted
     queue-item parameters remain editable for baked/static designs as well as
     parametric items; the nesting behavior flag does not hide fields. Bounded
     grid tracks and constrained layered previews prevent entry cards from
     stretching indefinitely without suppressing dimension or production
     drawing layers. The fixed fitted preview spans the left column; canonical
     source-template context and row actions lead the right column, with
     inline-labeled parameters below. Add Entry uses secondary emphasis.
   - Validation: generated overload/action/routing and project-file operation
     focused tests passed; changed SFCs parsed successfully; architecture,
     framework definition, and committed-manifest validation passed.

*** [2026-08-03] Brass Hands visual-system correction

    Reworked the app-level token contract from graphite/lime to an ink-and-
    near-white operational system with a sparse signal-orange action channel.
    `assets/tokens/index.js` and `assets/css/main.css` now own the matching
    palette, hard 3px/6px geometry, structural card borders, minimal elevation,
    uppercase utility-label tracking, and light/dark PrimeVue bridges. Shared
    entity-reference family tones and process-status severity tones now resolve
    through `entity-*` and `status-*` tokens instead of locally assigning
    primitive colors. Updated the assets, component, process-designer, and
    design-system documentation; focused design-system tests and the PrimeVue
    preset import passed before manifest regeneration.

    Follow-up browser verification replaced the non-painting inset signal
    shadow with the `chrome-signal-rule` token helper on both desktop/mobile
    app chrome and the UI-lab shell.

    Follow-up interaction correction: light-mode chrome now resolves to a
    near-white surface rather than the dark rail; structural card and workflow
    surfaces carry no elevation; and `EntityCard` uses an in-place primary
    hover border so its feedback remains visible within the required clipped
    card root. Overlay elevation is retained only for floating UI with a
    smaller, token-backed shadow.
